{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790264958,"nonce":"YXPM2dnji3KWPfPQG+wS/wL98QA=","title":"Bindgen: generate interface operations, callbacks and arbitrary unions from WebIDL","message":"The GPU plugin's API is complete, but much of it is still declared by hand in\n`gpu.api.rs` and converted by hand in `src/backend/`. Bindgen imports\ndictionaries, enums, constants, typedefs, records, nullable sequences and\ndeclared unions, and checks Promise returns. It does not yet:\n\n- generate interface operations, attributes, overloads and optional or\n  default arguments; resource traits are written out and only a\n  `#[idl(\"Interface.operation\")]` return is checked;\n- check operation parameters against the IDL, only returns;\n- project arbitrary multi-type unions to tagged Caribou values (only\n  unions declared as Rust enums, projected to one setter per alternative);\n- generate callback types and callback interfaces;\n- generate descriptor-to-wgpu conversions; `render.rs`, `copies.rs` and the\n  rest convert each record by hand;\n- carry ArrayBuffer views and browser image sources without copies;\n- keep `EnforceRange`, `Clamp` and exposure markers as validation rules.\n\nSplit out of e61c43c, which covered the API surface.","files":null}]}